/ #flash is rendered empty by the layout and replaced by a turbo_stream when
/ there is something to say. .flash carries `display: contents` because .op-page
/ is a grid and a real box here would displace the sidebar — see ui/flash.css.
/
/ The .popup is deliberately rendered WITHOUT .show: flash_controller adds it a
/ frame later so the notice animates in rather than appearing already arrived.
#flash.flash
  - if message.present?
    .popup data-controller="flash" data-action="click->flash#dismiss"
      p = message
